===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[spread]] (a substance, especially one that colours or is [[dirty]]) across a surface by [[rub]]bing.
#: {{syn|en|apply|daub|plaster|spread}}
#: {{ux|en|The artist '''smeared''' paint over the canvas in broad strokes.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1776|author=w:Oliver Goldsmith|title=A Survey of Experimental Philosophy|location=London|publisher=T. Carnan and F. Newbery|chapter=5|page=74|url=http://name.umdl.umich.edu/004897705.0001.001
|passage=In general, all bodies whose surfaces are even will {{...}} stick to each other, and if a liquid be '''smeared''' over either surface, their cohesion will be still the stronger.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2019|author=w:Ocean Vuong|title={{w|On Earth We're Briefly Gorgeous|On Earth We’re Briefly Gorgeous}}|url=https://books.google.ca/books?id=hKRtDwAAQBAJ&printsec=frontcover#v=onepage&q&f=false|publisher=Penguin|location=New York
|passage=Then you would kneel and '''smear''' a handful of pomade through my hair, comb it over.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To cover (a surface ''with'' a layer of some substance) by rubbing.
#: {{syn|en|bedaub|coat|cover|daub|layer|plaster}}
#: {{ux|en|She '''smeared''' her lips with lipstick.}}
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Macbeth|II|2|text=Why did you bring these daggers from the place?<br>They must lie there: go carry them; and '''smear'''<br>The sleepy grooms with blood.}}
#* {{RQ:Milton Paradise Lost|10 [11]|lines=725-727|text={{...}} a Vessel of huge bulk,<br>Measur’d by Cubit, length, & breadth, and highth,<br>'''Smeard''' round with Pitch,}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1964|author=w:Christopher Isherwood|title={{w|A Single Man (novel)|A Single Man}}|url=https://archive.org/details/singleman0000ishe/page/53/mode/1up?q=smear|page=53|publisher=Vintage|year_published=2010|location=London
|passage={{...}} it’s ''better'' if we admit to disliking and hating them, than if we try to '''smear''' our feelings over with pseudo-liberal sentimentality.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To make something dirty.
#: {{syn|en|besmirch|dirty|soil|sully}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1583|translator=w:Arthur Golding|title=The Sermons of {{w|John Calvin|M. John Calvin}} upon the {{w|Book of Deuteronomy|Fifth Book of Moses called Deuteronomie}}|location=London|publisher=George Bishop|section=Sermon 41, p. 246|url=http://name.umdl.umich.edu/A17698.0001.001
|passage=A man may bee '''smeared''' or grimed, and euerie man shall laugh at him, and yet he himselfe shall not perceiue it a whit.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1855|author=w:Elizabeth Gaskell|title={{w|North and South (Gaskell novel)|North and South}}|location=London|publisher=Chapman and Hall|volume=2|chapter=11|page=147|url=https://archive.org/details/northsouth02gask/page/147/mode/1up?q=smeared
|passage={{...}} she returned, carrying Johnnie, his face all '''smeared''' with eating,}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2016|author=w:Ali Smith|title={{w|Autumn (Smith novel)|Autumn}}|chapterurl=https://books.google.ca/books?id=A8AiDAAAQBAJ&printsec=frontcover#v=onepage&q&f=false|chapter=2|publisher=Penguin|year_published=2017
|passage=His hands and forearms, his face, his good shirt and suit are '''smeared''' from the dustbins and climbing the fence,}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} {{qualifier|of a substance, etc.}} To make a surface dirty by covering it.
#* {{RQ:Stoker Dracula|chapter=21|page=263|text=a pallor which was accentuated by the blood which '''smeared''' her lips and cheeks and chin}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1982|author=w:Anne Tyler|title=w:Dinner at the Homesick Restaurant|url=https://archive.org/details/dinnerathomesick0000tyle_x4u5/page/168/mode/1up?q=smear|chapter=6|page=168|publisher=Knopf|year_published=1989|location=New York
|passage=a rust spot '''smearing''' the back of the sink}}
#* {{RQ:Hollinghurst Line|chapter=12|page=323|passage=Wet leaves '''smeared''' the pavement.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[damage]] someone's [[reputation]] by [[slander]]ing, [[misrepresent]]ing, or otherwise making [[false]] [[accusation]]s about them, their statements, or their actions.
#: {{syn|en|badmouth|besmirch|defame|sully|vilify}}
#: {{ux|en|The opposition party attempted to '''smear''' the candidate by spreading incorrect and unverifiable rumors about their personal behavior.}}
#* {{RQ:Joyce Dubliners|{{w|Ivy Day in the Committee Room}}|page=164|text=May everlasting shame consume<br>The memory of those who tried<br>To befoul and '''smear''' th’ exalted name<br>Of one who spurned them in his pride.}}
#* '''1976''', {{w|Ngũgĩ wa Thiong'o}}, “J.M.—A Writer’s Tribute” in ''Writers in Politics,'' London: Heinemann, 1981, p.{{nbsp}}82,<sup>[https://archive.org/details/writersinpolitic0000ngug/page/82/mode/1up?q=smear]</sup>
#*: The imperialist foreigners then in the offices of the Nation Newspapers would not allow the African staff to review it. They handled it themselves in order to '''smear''' the book and its author and his celebration of {{w|Mau Mau Uprising|Mau Mau resistance}}.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2018|author=w:Richard Powers|title=w:The Overstory|location=New York|publisher=Norton|chapter=Neelay Mehta|url=https://books.google.ca/books?id=_zQsDwAAQBAJ&printsec=frontcover#v=onepage&q&f=false
|passage=They’ll '''smear''' him on the country’s dial-up bulletin boards as the worst traitor.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To cause (something) to be [[messy]] or not clear by rubbing and spreading it.
#: {{syn|en|blur|smudge}}
#* {{RQ:Dickens David Copperfield|44|page=457|text=When she had entered two or three laborious items in the account-book, Jip would walk over the page, wagging his tail, and '''smear''' them all out.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1954|author=w:J. R. R. Tolkien|title=w:The Fellowship of the Ring|location=New York|publisher=Ballantine|year_published=1973|section=Book 2, Chapter 5, p. 419|url=https://archive.org/details/lordofrings0000tolk_k7e8/page/419/mode/1up?q=smeared
|passage=Then there are four lines '''smeared''' so that I can only read ''went 5 days ago''.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2007|author=w:Tan Twan Eng|title=w:The Gift of Rain|location=New York|publisher=Weinstein Books|section=Book 1, Chapter 5, p. 56|url=https://archive.org/details/giftofrain00tant/page/56/mode/1up?q=smeared
|passage=Bird droppings, '''smeared''' by the strokes of rain and dried by the heat, streaked its sides.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To become messy or not clear by being spread.
#: {{syn|en|smudge}}
#: {{ux|en|The paint is still wet &mdash; don't touch it or it will '''smear'''.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[write]] or [[draw]] (something) by spreading a substance on a surface.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1970|author=w:Saul Bellow|title={{w|Mr. Sammler's Planet|Mr. Sammler’s Planet}}|location=New York|publisher=Fawcett|year_published=1971|chapter=2|page=84|url=https://archive.org/details/mrsammlersplanet1970bell/page/84/mode/1up?q=smeared
